  "updatedAt": 1791957447935,
  "sourceText": "# A line is not the whole story\n\nAn economic data visualization lesson. **All values below are simulated** and are not Nigerian official statistics.\n\n---\n\n# Start with the source\n\n| Period | Illustrative index |\n| --- | --- |\n| 2021 | 100 |\n| 2022 | 108 |\n| 2023 | 112 |\n| 2024 | 119 |\n\nAlways label the base period, unit, and source.\n\n---\n\n# Level and growth are different\n\n$$\ng_t=\\frac{I_t-I_{t-1}}{I_{t-1}}\\times100\n$$\n\nAn index level describes a position relative to a base. Growth describes a change between periods.\n\n---\n\n# Plot honestly\n\n- Use a clearly labeled time axis.\n- Explain any transformation.\n- Distinguish nominal and real values.\n- Do not infer causation from a trend alone.\n\n---\n\n# Ask one more question\n\nWhat changed in the measurement, coverage, or economic context?\n\nReplace simulated data with a verified source before making factual claims.\n\n[Source discovery: National Bureau of Statistics](https://www.nigerianstat.gov.ng/)",
